  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Resilience to Natural Disasters Risks in Burundi</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The general objective of the project is to contribute to strengthening the resilience of the Burundian population, thus helping to reduce chronic malnutrition in Burundi. The specific objective is to contribute to the consolidation of the disaster risk management system in Burundi. The project works in 18 provinces and 119 communes in Burundi to update risk maps and contingency plans. In doing so, target populations are better able and ready to deal with hazards and their impacts in terms of prevention, preparedness, and response. The project seeks three distinct results. Risk mapping will be made available and contributes to the review and/or development of contingency plans at different levels to take appropriate measures against natural disaster risks. Strengthening of institutional mechanisms contributes to better management and implementation of contingency plans and coordination of the actors concerned and involving communities in disaster risk reduction initiatives strengthens their resilience and their capacities for risk prevention and mitigation.</narrative>
  </description>
